The National Inquirer (ie: the source code) says:

Nope.  I've wondered about this myself, so I just checked the source code.

It only checks if the monster has the intrinsic, and then gives you a random
number.  If the monster's level is greater than the random number, then you
get the intrinsic.  This may explain why teleport control is so hard to get.
tengu's are only level 6 monsters, so your chances of getting it are only
so-so from a tengu corpse.

There is one level 30 monster with teleport control.  Eating it would almost
guarantee you'd get teleport control.  What's the monster?

Guess.



Here's a clue: Eating it would also give you aggravate monster.



Here's another clue:  There's only one in the whole game.  But you can
kill it and eat it several times.
